    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive engine. His 82.13 efficiency score is head-and-shoulders above the rest of the roster, fueled by a prime leadoff spot against the hittable Junk (xERA 4.67) and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage. In a category-scarcity environment, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides critical upside for stolen bases. Behind him, **Trea Turner** (64.77) and **Hector Rodriguez** (60.91) represent high-floor assets; **Hector Rodriguez** is particularly well-positioned to capitalize on a weak Ritchie (xERA 4.89) matchup despite batting lower in the order, while **Trea Turner** remains locked in as a stabilizer in the two-hole against May.\n\nWhile **Yordan Alvarez** (60.70) faces a challenging assignment against the elite arm of Gilbert, his 0.442 xwOBA dictates he remains a mandatory start regardless of the SP xERA. Conversely, the most difficult decision involved **Junior Caminero** (59.70). He nearly hit the 60-point threshold for a strong start, but his score was depressed by a poor BvP history against Fried and a disadvantageous platoon matchup. Ultimately, **Junior Caminero** earns the final UTIL spot over our deeper bench options due to his raw power, even as we monitor the health of **Colt Keith** and the rainouts of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**. \n\nManagement must remain cautious regarding the weather and roster availability. With **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** sidelined by postponements, our depth is significantly thinner than anticipated. Furthermore, **Christian Yelich** (52.08) is a marginal play against the elite arm of Wheeler (xERA 3.25); while he benefits from a dynamic platoon boost, his efficiency is limited by the matchup difficulty. Owners should monitor lineup updates for **Jacob Gonzalez**, who resides in the nine-hole; despite a decent score, his role at the bottom of the order and the tough task of facing Pallante makes him the most vulnerable member of the starting nine if late-game tactical adjustments are required.",
